tornado-spinner

This crate is a vendored copy of `ratatui-cheese` v0.7.0 — specifically,
the `crates/ratatui-cheese/src/spinner.rs` module — which provides a
Bubbletea-inspired spinner widget for the `ratatui` ecosystem.

Original source:
  Repository: https://github.com/shashanktomar/ratatui-cheese
  Sub-crate path: crates/ratatui-cheese (subcrate of a 2-crate workspace)
  Upstream crate: ratatui-cheese v0.7.0 on crates.io
  Authors:   Shashank Tomar
  License:   MIT (declared in upstream Cargo.toml)

Local changes:
  - Module lifted verbatim into the new `crates/tornado-spinner/src/spinner.rs`
    file under the arniko workspace. The vendored module has no internal
    references to other ratatui-cheese widgets or utilities — it depends
    only on `ratatui::buffer/Buffer`, `ratatui::layout/Rect`,
    `ratatui::style::{Style, Styled}`, and `ratatui::widgets::{Widget,
    StatefulWidget}` — so it ports without any rewiring beyond the
    parent crate rename.
  - Crate renamed to `tornado-spinner` for arniko workspace cohesion.
  - Edition inherited from the arniko workspace (`edition = "2024"`).
  - In the vendored code's inner doctest comments, the path
    `use ratatui_cheese::spinner::{...}` was rewritten to
    `use tornado_spinner::spinner::{...}` so the example in the rustdoc
    links to this crate's actual public path. (The doctest is otherwise
    valid because the underlying types are re-exported unchanged; the
    path is the only difference.)

License faithfulness:
  - The upstream repository declares `license = "MIT"` in
    `crates/ratatui-cheese/Cargo.toml` but does not ship a separate
    LICENSE file at the repo root. We reproduce the canonical MIT
    text here, attributing the copyright to "Shashank Tomar" for
    2026 (the year the upstream crate was first published). Use of
    the MIT text under the same terms as upstream is unaffected —
    the verbatim text in this file is the same MIT template that
    ships with reference MIT sources.

Co-composition with tornado's event loop:
  - `tornado::spinner::SpinnerState::tick(dt: Duration)` accepts the
    elapsed time of one `run_app` loop iteration and advances frames
    internally regardless of tick rate. The `TuiApp` shell can measure
    `dt = tick_start.elapsed()` each iteration (see
    `crates/tornado/src/lib.rs::run_loop`) and forward it to the
    spinner state once per tick, keeping animation cadence stable
    under variable host load.

Public path parity with upstream:
  - `ratatui_cheese::spinner::Spinner` → `tornado_spinner::spinner::Spinner`
  - `ratatui_cheese::spinner::SpinnerState` → `tornado_spinner::spinner::SpinnerState`
  - `ratatui_cheese::spinner::SpinnerType` → `tornado_spinner::spinner::SpinnerType`
  - All public methods, signatures, frame tables, and intervals are
    unchanged. The vendored test module exercises the full upstream
    surface — 29 unit tests covering presets, state, tick progression,
    wrapping, accumulation, and rendering. All pass under tornado's
    ratatui 0.30 pin.

Test departures from upstream:
  - None. The vendored `tests` module compiles and passes under
    `cargo test -p tornado-spinner` without modification.
